WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.670
- So we're celebrating music's
connection to civil rights.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.550
So, who were your social
musical inspirations?

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.770
- Nina Simone and Aretha Franklin.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.603
- [Kelly] Oh yeah, good.

00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:10.170
(audience applauding)

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.250
- [Kelly] Because they're like,

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.914
you know, some of the crème de crème.

00:00:12.914 --> 00:00:13.950
- Yeah.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.320
What I found out actually,
whilst I was learning

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.150
about both of them,'cause
I sing them a lot,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.500
I sing their music a lot,

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.177
is that Aretha was

00:00:21.177 --> 00:00:24.750
inspired by Nina Simone,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.850
and she ended up doing
a couple of the songs

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.920
that Nina Simone had on her albums.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.030
Young, Gifted and Black.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.863
- Yeah.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.160
- [Cynthia] You know, and obviously

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.920
Nina was very much in
the civil rights movement

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.190
and her music was about
that at some point.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.170
And they sort of met in the middle,

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.720
And both of those women are
huge inspirations for me.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.553
- [Kelly] Yeah,

00:00:43.553 --> 00:00:44.386
- Yeah.

00:00:44.386 --> 00:00:46.830
- [Kelly] It's interesting
'cause nobody thinks about it,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.630
but one, what was like the first time

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.190
you heard Aretha?

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.255
- I think I was,

00:00:51.255 --> 00:00:52.088
- [Kelly] First question.

00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:54.001
- I wanna say I was maybe 10 years old,

00:00:54.001 --> 00:00:56.880
in my mother's car on the way to school,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.070
and I think it was Chain of Fools.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.840
- [Kelly] Yeah, I think mine was around 13

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.150
and it was Respect or Chain of Fools,

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.440
I can't remember which one.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.150
But I just, there was something
different about her voice.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.899
- Isn't it? It just sort of like hits you,

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:10.860
right in the solar plexus.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.060
- Like just breaks you.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.070
- Yeah. And the tone...

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.540
But nobody really talks about this,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.118
but she actually did cover
quite a bit of music.

00:01:18.118 --> 00:01:18.951
- Yeah she did.

00:01:18.951 --> 00:01:19.784
- [Kelly] That was a lot of her career,

00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:20.617
which nobody really talked about.

00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:22.230
I feel like that's
maybe what influenced me

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.063
to do covers all the time,

00:01:23.063 --> 00:01:25.260
'cause I love it so much
and I love so many genres.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.390
- She had this wonderful, magical way of

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.090
making any song you may have heard,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.620
that belonged to someone else,

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.420
sound like it was already written for her

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.225
and they were just a
stepping stone to get to her.

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:36.058
- I thought that!

00:01:36.058 --> 00:01:36.927
So when I was a kid, I would listen to her

00:01:36.927 --> 00:01:37.980
and I was like, oh, I love her song

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.360
and they're like, you know that's a cover.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.200
Like, they did that originally.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.033
I was like, wait, what?

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.060
- [Cynthia] Respect is a cover!

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.740
- That's what I'm saying!
I never knew all those,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.970
I ended up finding that out

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:45.930
and I was like, I didn't...

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.300
- Oh, didn't know? Right. Special.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.089
- [Kelly] Nobody wanted
her to cover the song.

00:01:50.089 --> 00:01:50.983
(crowd laughing)

00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:51.816
- [Cynthia] Oh no.

00:01:51.816 --> 00:01:52.770
- Because then it was gone,

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.033
it was not yours anymore.

